    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a per-day owner-creation limit on `POST /api/owners`: once 100 or more owners have already been created today (by `registrationDate`), the request is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**. I followed the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, mirroring the existing `CheckCityCapacity` check.\n\n**New files:**\n- `CheckDailyLimit.java` (function/owner) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`; throws `DailyLimitExceededException` at `DAILY_LIMIT = 100`.\n- `DailyLimitExceededException.java` (escalation) \u2014 checked exception carrying the limit.\n- `DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` (escalation) \u2014 responds 429 with an RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` using the shared `ProblemDetails` helper.\n- `...DailyLimitExceededException.yml` (escalation) \u2014 routes the exception to the handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step (under `transaction` governance) between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`.\n\n**Result:** `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect 101st \u2192 429) passes, and the full `mvn test` build is green.",
